# L §5.9 Rows replaced: replace rows that "all take intervals of the table they replace" leave "that table ... with
# those rows' values replaced", applied "to the table in force on each day". L5_9_patch_no_table_load with v2 governing
# 2027 only, inside v1's span: it loads; in 2027 b(15) lies in (10, 20], which v2 doesn't patch: 2 (q1); in 2028 no
# table is in force: a hole (q2, L §4.6 step 5); in 2026 v1's, 2 (q3).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2027-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2028-12-31

source s "s"
band b(n: int): int
input mid: int

version v1
  cite s
  governs 2026..2027
  known 2025-12-01
  b: [0, 10] = 1
  b: (10, 20] = 2
  b: (20, inf) = 3

version facts
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  mid = 15

version v2
  cite s
  governs 2027
  known 2026-12-01
  replace b: [0, 10] = 5
  replace b: (20, inf) = 6

ask q1: b(mid) law 2027-06-30
ask q2: b(mid) law 2028-06-30
ask q3: b(mid) law 2026-06-30
=== expect
q1: 2
  law date 2027-06-30, cut 2027-01-01
q2: ?"b: no value at 2028-06-30" (b)
  law date 2028-06-30, cut 2027-01-01
q3: 2
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2027-01-01
